{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:c157d1597a73913a","name":"Blind Descent","source":{"id":"source:reference-c157d1597a73913a","title":"Blind Descent","revision":16290,"timestamp":"2024-08-18T00:56:37Z","sha256":"210607b407e9e07149785927d32fc44e4828179321a4667b231779475e0fc004","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=16290","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Blind%20Descent&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-c157d1597a73913a","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Galaxy of Intrigue"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Galaxy_of_Intrigue"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Should the heroes attempt to make a Blind Descent into ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nyriaan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nyriaan","referenceId":"reference:ffb4373927de3433"},", there is a significant chance that they will not make it down safely. The descent is tough, even for veteran pilots, and the risk of failure also brings with it the promise of a crash landing. However, if the heroes are foolhardy (or simply desperate) enough to attempt a Blind Descent into ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nyriaan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nyriaan","referenceId":"reference:ffb4373927de3433"}," without the advantage of any of the planet's normal technology, use the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Challenge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Challenge"}," below to determine the outcome of their descent.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Blind Descent Statistics (CL 12)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Complexity:"]}," 2 (8 Successes before 3 Failures)\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"},":"]}," The following are suggested Primary Skills for this ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Challenge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Challenge"},":\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," (DC 31):"]}," While the ship makes its descent, heroes aboard the ship can make ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," checks to boost power to shields and internal system buffers, reducing the chances that the ship will suffer a blackout during its approach."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," (DC 31):"]}," The heroes can use ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," to watch out for stray bolts of energy discharging through the atmosphere, warning the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," when it looks like things are going to get rough up ahead."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pilot","referenceId":"reference:383e2d946278a872"}," (DC 26):"]}," The ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," of the ship can try to bring the vessel down on a safe course using instinct and natural skill to guide the craft."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," (DC 21):"]}," A hero can use the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," skill to calculate trajectories, anticipate wind and energy discharge powers, and try to boost sensors to provide the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," with at least some data with regards to their descent."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Use the Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_the_Force","referenceId":"reference:74883d1dd46b87fe"}," (DC 35):"]}," Force-sensitive heroes can use the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use the Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_the_Force","referenceId":"reference:74883d1dd46b87fe"}," skill to sense danger in the descent, but the strange atmospheric effects of the planet make this a tricky proposition at best."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Challenge Effects"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The following are suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Challenge Effects"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Challenge_Effects"}," for this ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Challenge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Challenge"},":\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Catastrophic Failure"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Catastrophic_Failure","referenceId":"reference:8e66c70d3771541a"},":"]}," If a hero fails a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Check"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Check"}," by 10 or more, the heroes accrue two Failures instead of one."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Degrees of Failure"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Degrees_of_Failure","referenceId":"reference:8d28a4bee6e70b14"},":"]}," The final outcome of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Challenge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Challenge"}," depends on the number of Failures accrued during the entirety of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Challenge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Challenge"},"."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Second Effort"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Second_Effort","referenceId":"reference:a3fb2d61f7258bdf"},":"]}," Whenever the heroes accrue a Failure, they can choose to instead have their ship move -1 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Persistent"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Persistent"}," step down the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Condition Track"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Condition_Track"},", and turn that Failure into a Success."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Success and Failure"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Success:"]}," When the heroes have achieved their eighth Success in the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Challenge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Challenge"},", they make it safely to the ground. However, depending on the number of Failures they have accrued (and the number of times they had to use the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Second Effort"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Second_Effort","referenceId":"reference:a3fb2d61f7258bdf"}," Challenge Effect), their ship may not be in very good condition.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Failure:"]}," Each time the heroes accrue a Failure, their ship ends up landing more and more off-course. Each time the party accrues a Failure, their ship takes 5d10x2 damage. If the challenge ends with 1 Failure, the ship lands 1d10 km off-course. If the challenge ends with 2 Failures, the ship lands 3d10 km off-course. If the heroes fail the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Challenge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Challenge"},", the ship crash lands 5d10 km off-course, and the ship is automatically reduced to 0 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},". The heroes each take 3d10x2 damage from the crash.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
